{"entries":[{"id":"tsk-job-7-1","title":"Job 7:1","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"JOB","chapterStart":7,"verseStart":1,"chapterEnd":7,"verseEnd":1},"content":"<p>1 Job excuses his desire of death. 12 He complains of his own restlessness, and expostulates with God.</p>\n<p>Is there. 14:5,13,14; Ps 39:4; Isa 38:5; Joh 11:9,10 an appointed time. or, a warfare. Ec 8:8 like the days. 14:6; Le 25:50; De 15:18; Isa 21:16; Mt 20:1-15</p>"},{"id":"tsk-job-7-2","title":"Job 7:2","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"JOB","chapterStart":7,"verseStart":2,"chapterEnd":7,"verseEnd":2},"content":"<p>ernestly desireth. Heb. gapeth after. Ps 119:131; 143:6 the shadow. Jer 6:4 as an hireling. Le 19:13; De 24:15; Mal 3:5; Jas 5:4</p>"},{"id":"tsk-job-7-3","title":"Job 7:3","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"JOB","chapterStart":7,"verseStart":3,"chapterEnd":7,"verseEnd":3},"content":"<p>months of. 29:2; Ps 6:6; 39:5; Ec 1:14</p>"},{"id":"tsk-job-7-4","title":"Job 7:4","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"JOB","chapterStart":7,"verseStart":4,"chapterEnd":7,"verseEnd":4},"content":"<p>When. 13,14; 17:12; 30:17; De 28:67; Ps 6:6; 77:4; 130:6 night, etc. Heb. evening be measured. tossings. Ps 109:23; Isa 54:11</p>"},{"id":"tsk-job-7-5","title":"Job 7:5","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"JOB","chapterStart":7,"verseStart":5,"chapterEnd":7,"verseEnd":5},"content":"<p>flesh. 2:7,8; 17:14; 19:26; 24:20; 30:18,19; Ps 38:5-7; Isa 1:6; 14:11 Ac 12:23 loathsome. 9:31; Isa 66:24; Eze 20:43</p>"},{"id":"tsk-job-7-6","title":"Job 7:6","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"JOB","chapterStart":7,"verseStart":6,"chapterEnd":7,"verseEnd":6},"content":"<p>swifter. 9:25; 16:22; 17:11; Ps 90:5,6; 102:11; 103:15,16; 144:4 Isa 38:12,13; 40:6,7; Jas 1:11; 4:14; 1Pe 1:24 without hope. 6:11; 17:15; Pr 14:32; Jer 2:25; Eph 2:12; 1Pe 1:13</p>"},{"id":"tsk-job-7-7","title":"Job 7:7","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"JOB","chapterStart":7,"verseStart":7,"chapterEnd":7,"verseEnd":7},"content":"<p>remember. 10:9; Ge 42:36; Ne 1:8; Ps 74:18,22; 89:47,50; Jer 15:15 my life. Ps 78:39; Jas 4:14 no more see. Heb. not return to see, that is, to enjoy. 10:21,22</p>"},{"id":"tsk-job-7-8","title":"Job 7:8","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"JOB","chapterStart":7,"verseStart":8,"chapterEnd":7,"verseEnd":8},"content":"<p>The eye. 20:9; Ps 37:36 thine eyes. 13:27; 14:3; Ps 39:11; 90:8,9 I am not. that is, I can live no longer. 21</p>"},{"id":"tsk-job-7-9","title":"Job 7:9","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"JOB","chapterStart":7,"verseStart":9,"chapterEnd":7,"verseEnd":9},"content":"<p>the cloud. 37:11 he. 10:21; 14:10-14; 16:22; 2Sa 12:23; 14:14; Ps 39:13; Isa 38:11</p>"},{"id":"tsk-job-7-10","title":"Job 7:10","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"JOB","chapterStart":7,"verseStart":10,"chapterEnd":7,"verseEnd":10},"content":"<p>shall return. 8:18; 20:9; Ps 103:16</p>"},{"id":"tsk-job-7-11","title":"Job 7:11","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"JOB","chapterStart":7,"verseStart":11,"chapterEnd":7,"verseEnd":11},"content":"<p>I will not. 6:26; 10:1; 13:13; 16:6; 21:3; Ps 39:3; 40:9 the anguish. Ge 42:21; 2Ki 4:27,28; Mt 26:37,38; Lu 22:44; 2Co 2:4 the bitterness. 10:15; 21:25; 1Sa 1:10; Isa 38:15,17</p>"},{"id":"tsk-job-7-12","title":"Job 7:12","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"JOB","chapterStart":7,"verseStart":12,"chapterEnd":7,"verseEnd":12},"content":"<p>I a sea. 17; 38:6-11; La 3:7 a whale. 41:1-34</p>"},{"id":"tsk-job-7-13","title":"Job 7:13","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"JOB","chapterStart":7,"verseStart":13,"chapterEnd":7,"verseEnd":13},"content":"<p>My bed. 3,4; 9:27,28; Ps 6:6; 77:4</p>"},{"id":"tsk-job-7-14","title":"Job 7:14","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"JOB","chapterStart":7,"verseStart":14,"chapterEnd":7,"verseEnd":14},"content":"<p>thou scarest. Ge 40:5-7; 41:8; Jud 7:13,14; Da 2:1; Mt 27:19</p>"},{"id":"tsk-job-7-15","title":"Job 7:15","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"JOB","chapterStart":7,"verseStart":15,"chapterEnd":7,"verseEnd":15},"content":"<p>chooseth. 2Sa 17:23; Mt 27:5 life. Heb. bones.</p>"},{"id":"tsk-job-7-16","title":"Job 7:16","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"JOB","chapterStart":7,"verseStart":16,"chapterEnd":7,"verseEnd":16},"content":"<p>I loathe it. 3:20-22; 6:9; 10:1; Ge 27:46; 1Ki 19:4; Jon 4:3,8 let me alone. 10:20; 14:6; Ps 39:10,13 my days. Ps 62:9; 78:33; 144:4; Ec 6:11,12</p>"},{"id":"tsk-job-7-17","title":"Job 7:17","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"JOB","chapterStart":7,"verseStart":17,"chapterEnd":7,"verseEnd":17},"content":"<p>What is man. Ps 8:4; 144:3; Heb 2:6 magnify. 12; 1Sa 24:14 set thine. 34:14,15</p>"},{"id":"tsk-job-7-18","title":"Job 7:18","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"JOB","chapterStart":7,"verseStart":18,"chapterEnd":7,"verseEnd":18},"content":"<p>visit. Ex 20:5; 32:34; Isa 26:14; 38:12,13 try. Ge 22:1; De 8:16; Jer 9:7; Da 12:10; Zec 13:9; 1Pe 1:7</p>"},{"id":"tsk-job-7-19","title":"Job 7:19","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"JOB","chapterStart":7,"verseStart":19,"chapterEnd":7,"verseEnd":19},"content":"<p>How long. 9:18; Ps 6:3; 13:1-3; 94:3; Re 6:10</p>"},{"id":"tsk-job-7-20","title":"Job 7:20","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"JOB","chapterStart":7,"verseStart":20,"chapterEnd":7,"verseEnd":20},"content":"<p>I have sinned. 9:29-31; 13:26; 14:16; 22:5; 31:33; 33:9,27; Ps 80:4 O thou preserver. Ne 9:6; Ps 36:6 why hast. 12; 6:4; 16:12-14; Ps 21:12; La 3:12 I am. 11; 3:24</p>"},{"id":"tsk-job-7-21","title":"Job 7:21","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"JOB","chapterStart":7,"verseStart":21,"chapterEnd":7,"verseEnd":21},"content":"<p>why dost. 10:14; 13:23,24; Isa 64:9; La 3:42-44; 5:20-22 take away. 2Sa 24:10; Mic 7:18,19; Ho 14:2; Joh 1:29; Tit 2:14; 1Jo 1:9; 3:5 sleep. 3:13; 17:14; 21:32,33; Ec 12:7; Isa 26:19; Da 12:2 in the morning. 18 but I shall not be. Ps 37:36; 103:15</p>"}]}